  "definitions": {
   "launches": "pump.fun mints created that UTC day and seen by our capture",
   "graduated": "true graduation under our label rules: the bonding curve completed, or a migration was seen while the curve was near completion; fake pools do not count",
   "instant_graduations": "true graduations whose migration was seen within 2 s of launch: the mint was created, filled and migrated in one bundle, before anyone outside it could trade",
   "organic_graduations": "every other true graduation (including the few with no migration timing)",
   "median_s_to_graduation_all": "median seconds from launch to the first migration sighting over true graduations with timing",
   "median_s_to_graduation_organic": "the same median over organic graduations",
   "rug_within_300s_rate": "share of launches our rug classification flagged within 300 s of launch (drain from a meaningful peak)",
   "creator_sold_within_60s_share": "share of launches whose creator's first sell came within 60 s of launch",
   "ticker_copies": "7-day window, tickers compared case-insensitively: for each organic graduate, the number of other mints launched in the same 7 days with the same ticker; top_launched_tickers = the most launched tickers of those 7 days",
   "settling": "the dataset export rebuilds its last three days nightly because outcomes settle late; those numbers can still change",
   "pools": "the PumpSwap pools our capture saw open that UTC day with 50 SOL or more, five or more trades in their first 30 minutes and no gap in our reading of them (recorded by chainstack/pool_outcomes.py): lost_90pct_in_30m = the pool price at the last trade inside those 30 minutes was at or below a tenth of the price at the first trade; median_s_to_collapse = seconds from the pool's opening to the first price at or below that tenth; observations of what happened, not a forecast",
   "by_kind": "the same counts per kind of launch, read from each launch's own curve account on the chain. classic = quoted in SOL and not mayhem mode: the kind our graduation and rug labels fully describe, and the denominator to use for a graduation rate. mayhem = a SOL-quoted mayhem-mode launch (an opt-in setting in which pump.fun's own agent may trade the coin): a few percent of them are marked complete on the chain with reserves far below the 85 SOL of a graduation (complete_on_chain), which is not a graduation under our rules. other_quote = quoted in another asset, mayhem mode or not (tokenized stocks, PUMP, USDC, PYUSD, other coins; since 2026-09-10): measured in SOL our labels do not apply, so complete_on_chain is the one outcome given. The headline rates above divide by ALL launches, as they always have",
   "label_check": "our graduated label against the curve account's own `complete` flag on classic launches (see /v1/datasets/schema/pumpfun_launches)"
  },
